  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, says his favourite theory is one he credits to Jacques Vallée, a veteran UFO researcher, and Diana Pasulka, a scholar who writes about religion and UFO belief. As Michels tells it, the theory holds that the 1947 crash near Roswell, New Mexico, where something is said to have come down on a ranch, was a dividing line: before it, people described strange beings in the language of folklore, and after it, they described them as aliens. If true, it would mean the same phenomenon simply changed its costume to suit the times."
